.LONG TERM...
Issued at 103 PM PST Sat Nov 14 2026
(Monday through next Friday)

Another break in rainfall is expected late in the day on Monday
and into Tuesday with a mix of sun and clouds. By Tuesday morning,
there is the potential for cold weather products (Frost
Advisories and/or Cold Weather Advisories) as morning lows are
forecast to be in 30s across the North Bay Valleys, southern
Salinas Valley, and 40s elsewhere across the Bay Area and Central
Coast.

Yet another system comes into the region Tuesday
afternoon/evening and moves southward across the north Central
Coast through Wednesday and potentially lingering into early
Friday morning. It is still too early to speak about rainfall
amounts, yet there is increasing confidence (as of this writing)
of higher rainfall amounts compared to the Sunday/Monday system.
There also appears to be greater potential for thunderstorms and
stronger winds ahead of the frontal boundary. Best written by my
colleague: "The flooding concerns will increase through the next
few days as soils saturate and creeks and streams reach bankfull.
Beyond the seven-day outlook, the weather pattern remains active
with a lean towards rain totals above seasonal averages into the
last week of November.

