.MARINE...
(Today through Thursday)
Issued at 908 AM PST Sat Nov 14 2026

Moderate to fresh southerly breezes will develop over the waters
as a cold front approaches from the north today. Fresh to strong
breezes will develop tonight and early Sunday as the cold front
moves through. Very hazardous marine conditions persist into
early next week with high west- northwest seas up to 30 feet.
Wave heights subside slightly on Sunday, but rebuild to high seas
with the frontal passage. Expect wave enhancement near harbor
entrances and bars due to shoaling. Widespread rain returns
Sunday morning and continues into Monday as moderate northwest
winds settle over the coastal waters.

